course: dictionary
lesson: 12944
title: Going over the limit
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Exceed means to go above a limit or amount. Exceeding is the -ing form of exceed, so it means going above a limit. «The lorry was exceeding the speed limit.» That means it was going faster than the limit allowed. To check, ask: is the number bigger than the limit? If yes, it is exceeding it.
explain: Not exceeding means "no more than". «The bag must weigh a weight not exceeding 10 kilograms.» So 10 kilograms is allowed, and anything lighter is allowed too, but 11 kilograms is not. Here, not exceeding means "10 or less".
explain: Exceeding also has an old, formal meaning: very great. «The queen showed exceeding kindness to the children.» Here it does not mean going over a limit. It means the kindness was very great. Exceedingly means extremely, as in «The soup was exceedingly hot.»
fact: Exceed means to go above a limit or amount.
fact: «Exceeding the speed limit» means going faster than the speed limit allows.
fact: «Not exceeding» means no more than, so 100 is allowed and 101 is not.
fact: In maths, «exceeding 100» means more than 100, but not 100 itself.
fact: «Exceedingly» means extremely. In road safety, exceeding the speed limit is dangerous and against the law.
exercise: «The driver was exceeding the speed limit of 30.» What does exceeding mean here? | Going slower than 30 | *Going faster than 30 | Parked by the school gate | Stopped at the traffic lights
exercise: «The bag must weigh a weight not exceeding 10 kilograms.» What does not exceeding 10 kilograms mean? | *10 kilograms or less | Any weight at all | Exactly 11 kilograms | More than 10 kilograms
exercise: Maths question: which number is exceeding 100? | *101 | 50 | 100 | 99
test: «Her teacher showed exceeding patience with the whole class.» What does exceeding mean here? | Less than usual | Going over a limit | Lost and confused | *Very great
test: Which phrase means "no more than 5"? | *Not exceeding 5 | Exceeding 5 | Exactly 6 | Above 5
exam: Ruby says exceeding the speed limit is fine if you are only a little over. What is the right answer? | *Exceeding the speed limit is dangerous and against the law, even a little | It is always allowed for a careful driver | It only means driving more slowly | It is fine if you are only a little over
